Implemented and executed in the focused environments:

- RFC 9580 v6 fingerprint/salt parsing and negative vectors; complete-key identities.
- purpose-separated `MRML-GIT-HYBRID-V1` AND verification and bounded trust transitions.
- ML-DSA self-verification, runtime entropy wrappers, malformed-key rejection, and volatile clearing of reviewed secret-derived intermediates.
- bounded Git object/pack/index parsing, deterministic fixed-Huffman LZ77 DEFLATE, file-backed quarantine validation, OFS/REF delta resolution, authenticated thin-base completion, arrival packs, disk reservation, journals, atomic ref generations, recovery classification, and authenticated audit receipts.
- deterministic verification of every introduced commit, including merge-side ancestry, concrete detached hybrid proofs, and protected activation that consumes opaque verified state.
- canonical monotonic pair-validity/retirement state, authenticated purpose-separated key revocations, and generation-bound verification summaries derived only from opaque verified commit proofs.
- canonical full-fingerprint legacy-v4 validity/retirement/revocation policy state; policy membership alone remains inert and cannot bypass graph classification.
- bounded checkpoint/cutover graph classification with a valid conventional-v4 signature bound to exact commit bytes, complete fingerprint, trusted signing time, repository, and generations; every non-checkpoint-ancestry commit still requires hybrid evidence.
- canonical bounded pack-set manifests and an `MRREFS02` transition that atomically binds the exact manifest digest while advancing repository and pack generations; hosted receive cumulatively persists the selected set and reauthenticates exact selected arrival objects for subsequent thin bases.
- sequential protected receive history traversal over prior selected arrivals; the focused test prepares a second commit whose parent exists only in the first activated arrival generation.
- bounded annotated-tag pages/details and verified metadata descriptors for exact source-manifest, source-lock, and build-receipt blobs without assuming ambient host paths or unsigned filename authority.
- bounded protocol-v2 request parsing, `ls-refs`, fetch framing, receive command/report framing, and repository-view boundaries without an external Git server runtime.
- deterministic bounded hostile-input corpora for Git pack/index/object/transport/trust/journal/ref-state/name/path parsers, OpenPGP packet/armor parsing, and ML-DSA key/signature verification on Linux and the Wine-hosted Windows target.
- six simultaneous process-local Linux fetch-pack generations from one immutable object graph, all byte-identical to the independently generated expected pack.
- conservative pre-body disk admission at the exact 2 GiB incoming-pack limit and fail-closed rejection at 2 GiB plus one byte, without allocating or consuming a body. This is boundary/admission evidence, not a completed 2 GiB stream or storage-performance run.

Explicit blockers (`REMAINS_OPEN`):

- Dynamic-Huffman level-9 canonical encoding, bounded delta selection, cross-pack recomputation, pack caching, and compaction await the required mechanism-level Canadian patent review and CIPO verification recorded in `PATENT_SCREEN.md`; they were not bypassed.
- The normal installed-as-`git` commit/tag paths do not yet use the complete protected detached-proof transaction end to end. Pull now authenticates and fully traverses its isolated candidate before installation and accepts the exact `--ff-only` spelling, but production trust-policy proof retrieval remains open.
- Production durable detached-proof storage/key-service integration, general repository-view/upload-pack composition over selected arrival objects, canonical compaction generation switching, and concurrent thin receive tests remain open.
- Authenticated emergency-recovery execution remains open; normal rotation and canonical key revocation cannot substitute for that separately pinned authority.
- Itemized FIPS 204 errata mapping, constant-time timing evidence, and independent cryptographic/security review remain open. The checked-in mandatory NIST ACVP and independent OpenSSL interoperability fixtures pass on Linux and the Wine-hosted Windows target.
- Native Windows directory durability, process-kill fault injection at every durable boundary, power-loss/physical-storage evidence, coverage-guided sanitizer/fuzz campaigns beyond the deterministic mutation corpus, multiprocess/distributed concurrency and peak-memory benchmarks, and production performance measurements remain open. Exact functional history-limit cases and process-local thread concurrency are covered, but do not satisfy those broader evidence requirements.
- Repository-specific release metadata discovery conventions, richer standard command forms, complete upload-pack negotiation/caching, and production receive-pack edge composition remain partial. Exact annotated tags and caller-selected verified source-manifest/source-lock/build-receipt blobs are available without filename-based authority. Unsupported capability paths remain fail closed and are not advertised.
- Assurance remains red for the unrelated unadmitted compiler probe identified above.

